{
  "name": "uft_shared_resume",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "steps": [
    {
      "comment": "Issue #11, live. A real craft loop — real pawns, real DoBill jobs, real ingredients — for an order that leaves an unfinished item behind, in a two-bench shared list. The bench roles in every probe are 0 = anchor (owns the list), 1 = member, -1 = neither, -2 = nothing to report. The resume rule under test: stay at the bench the item is parked at while it is usable, and move to a free linked bench only when it is not.",
      "type": "SetTime",
      "args": {
        "hour": "9"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetTerrain",
      "args": {
        "def": "Concrete",
        "width": "20",
        "height": "20"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "PlaceThings",
      "args": {
        "def": "HandTailoringBench",
        "layout": "cells",
        "cells": "-4,0; 4,0",
        "rot": "North"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgClaimBenches",
      "args": {
        "def": "HandTailoringBench"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgLinkBenches",
      "args": {
        "def": "HandTailoringBench",
        "limit": "2"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_group_size",
        "expectedValue": "2",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_redirect_installed",
        "expectedValue": "1",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "Negative path first, on the empty list: bills that genuinely cannot be shared still bounce off AddBill, now that they share IsShareableBill with the ones that can. Lifter is a Bill_ProductionMech (gestation), ResurrectLightMech a Bill_ResurrectMech. Both Biotech; ifPresent logs a skip on a machine without it.",
      "type": "WbgTryAddBill",
      "args": {
        "recipe": "Lifter",
        "expect": "refused",
        "ifPresent": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgTryAddBill",
      "args": {
        "recipe": "ResurrectLightMech",
        "expect": "refused",
        "ifPresent": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_bills_visible_at_second_bench",
        "expectedValue": "0",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "The positive half of the gate: a Bill_ProductionWithUft goes into the shared list and is visible from the member.",
      "type": "WbgTryAddBill",
      "args": {
        "recipe": "Make_Apparel_BasicShirt",
        "expect": "added"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_bills_visible_at_second_bench",
        "expectedValue": "1",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgSpawnStack",
      "args": {
        "def": "Cloth",
        "count": "75",
        "cell": "0,-3"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgSpawnStack",
      "args": {
        "def": "Steel",
        "count": "10",
        "cell": "0,-6",
        "role": "control"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgMakeStockpile",
      "args": {
        "from": "-2,4",
        "to": "2,6",
        "allow": "Steel, UnfinishedApparel"
      },
      "comment": "Accepts only the control steel and the unfinished item, so the hauler's window is spent on the two things under test rather than the fixture colony's junk. Accepting the unfinished item is what makes 'left alone' a finding: the stockpile would take it."
    },
    {
      "type": "SpawnPawn",
      "args": {
        "kind": "Colonist",
        "count": "4",
        "faction": "player",
        "offset": "-3,-9",
        "spacing": "2"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgAssignRoles",
      "args": {}
    },
    {
      "comment": "Phase 1: the member is busy, so the crafter starts the order at the anchor. The unfinished item appears there.",
      "type": "WbgOccupyBench",
      "args": {
        "which": "member"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "FastForward",
      "args": {
        "ticks": "900"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_crafter_job_at",
        "expectedValue": "0",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_uft_count",
        "expectedValue": "1",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_uft_at",
        "expectedValue": "0",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "Interrupted: drafted mid-craft, the item stays on the anchor. Then the anchor becomes the busy one.",
      "type": "WbgDraft",
      "args": {
        "drafted": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgRememberUft",
      "args": {}
    },
    {
      "comment": "Phase 2a: nothing is busy. Asked from the member, the real work giver still sends the pawn back to the anchor, because that is where the item is parked and the anchor is usable. The job should not move just because a different bench was scanned first.",
      "type": "WbgOccupyBench",
      "args": {
        "which": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_resume_target_at",
        "expectedValue": "0",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgDraft",
      "args": {
        "drafted": "false"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "FastForward",
      "args": {
        "ticks": "500"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_crafter_job_at",
        "expectedValue": "0",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_uft_same_item",
        "expectedValue": "1",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_uft_at",
        "expectedValue": "0",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "Interrupted again at the anchor. Now the anchor is the busy one, so phase 2b must move the job.",
      "type": "WbgDraft",
      "args": {
        "drafted": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgOccupyBench",
      "args": {
        "which": "anchor"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "The transpiler's answer, asked directly of the real work giver: from the free member, the resume job targets the member. Vanilla targets the anchor here (see uft_shared_resume_control).",
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_resume_target_at",
        "expectedValue": "1",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "Phase 2: let the pawn's own think tree choose. It must resume the same item at the free member, carrying it over, while the bill still belongs to the anchor.",
      "type": "WbgDraft",
      "args": {
        "drafted": "false"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "FastForward",
      "args": {
        "ticks": "700"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_crafter_job_at",
        "expectedValue": "1",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_crafter_job_vanilla_at",
        "expectedValue": "0",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_uft_same_item",
        "expectedValue": "1",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_uft_count",
        "expectedValue": "1",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_uft_at",
        "expectedValue": "1",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "Phase 3: interrupted again, so the item is parked at the member. Vanilla's anchor-only guard does not cover it there; ours does, and BoundWorkTable names the member.",
      "type": "WbgDraft",
      "args": {
        "drafted": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgOccupyBench",
      "args": {
        "which": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_uft_at",
        "expectedValue": "1",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_uft_vanilla_guard",
        "expectedValue": "0",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_uft_haulable",
        "expectedValue": "0",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_uft_bound_table_at",
        "expectedValue": "1",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgCloseDebugLog",
      "args": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "Select",
      "args": {
        "defName": "UnfinishedApparel",
        "count": "1"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "LookAt",
      "args": {
        "zoom": "13"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Wait",
      "args": {
        "frames": "20"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Screenshot",
      "args": {
        "fileName": "uft_parked_at_member.png",
        "hideUi": "false"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "A hauler with nothing else to do, a stockpile that accepts everything, and a control stack of steel. The steel reaching the stockpile proves the hauler hauls; the item staying at the member proves it was left alone on purpose.",
      "type": "WbgEnableWork",
      "args": {
        "role": "hauler",
        "workType": "Hauling"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "FastForward",
      "args": {
        "ticks": "5000"
      },
      "comment": "Long enough for a randomly generated hauler to finish carrying the leftover cloth as well as the control steel; 2500 ticks passed on one pawn and not on the next."
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_control_in_storage",
        "expectedValue": "1",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_uft_at",
        "expectedValue": "1",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "Phase 4: back to work, and the order finishes — the product is real, not just a job that pointed somewhere.",
      "type": "WbgDraft",
      "args": {
        "drafted": "false"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgLogCrafter",
      "args": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "FastForward",
      "args": {
        "ticks": "10000"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgLogCrafter",
      "args": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_first_bill_remaining",
        "expectedValue": "0",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_uft_count",
        "expectedValue": "0",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    }
  ]
}
